From 88455fb911bb873772bad56dd100045b2a4fc81f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kierandrewett <kieran@drewett.dev>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:07:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] x11: remove the frame window code

Nothing creates an X11 frame window any more: the compositor frames managed
windows, so MetaWindowX11Private::frame is always NULL. Remove the MetaFrame
type and every path that handled a frame window: its borders, sync counter,
opaque region and configure handling, the stack and focus bookkeeping for a
second toplevel, the client reparenting counters that only the frame used,
the frame mask in the X11 window actor, the _MUTTER_FRAME_FOR,
_MUTTER_FRAME_EXTENTS and _MUTTER_NEEDS_FRAME atoms, and MetaFrameBorders.

meta_frame_type_to_string stays because the X11 window actor picks its shadow
class with it. meta_window_x11_get_toplevel_xwindow was the client window
whenever there was no frame, so its one test caller uses
meta_window_x11_get_xwindow.

constrain_to_single_monitor only applied to X11 windows that had a frame
window. It now never applies, as before for every other window.
